# OS / editor
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp
.idea/
.vscode/

# Secrets / local env — never commit
.env
.env.*
*.pem
aws.json
warehouse.env
isp_proxies.txt
**/isp_proxies.txt

# Claude Code — skills are committed; machine-local settings/state are not
.claude/settings.local.json
.claude/launch.json
.claude/worktrees/

# Python (unifyd engine)
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/

# Unifyd engine runtime — pulled data + agent state never go in git
unifyd/agent_state/
unifyd/cola_out/
unifyd/out/
unifyd/**/*.local.json
cola_labels.csv
*.log

# (kept in git on purpose: unifyd/fixtures/ — parser reference pages)
unifyd/walmart_sched.log

# runtime scraper output (not source)
unifyd/full_out/
unifyd/specs_out/
unifyd/walmart_raw/
unifyd/full_pull_out/

# Scraper state snapshots — runtime, not source. .dockerignore has excluded these since the image
# was first built (`**/*_snapshot.json`), but .gitignore did not, so they sat untracked and
# committable: unifyd/binnys_snapshot.json alone is 11GB. One `git add -A` would have put it in the
# history permanently. Mirror the dockerignore rule.
unifyd/*_snapshot.json

# iCloud copy-collision artefacts. This repo lives under the synced Desktop folder, and when iCloud
# resolves a conflict it writes a sibling named "<name> 2.<ext>" (or "<name> 2" for a directory).
# They are never source, and they have caused real damage — not hypothetically, all on 2026-08-03:
#   · "salsify 2.py" was committed to main by a `git add -A` and had to be removed in #773
#   · duplicated refs (".git/refs/heads/<branch> 2") broke `git fetch` outright, which silently
#     made a deploy ship a STALE tree while every release still read `complete`
#   · "poll_ue_progress 2.py" carried pre-fix code and failed a guard in the working directory
#     while a clean checkout of the same commit passed
# This stops them entering the history. It does NOT stop the .git/refs corruption — nothing in
# .gitignore can, since git does not consult it for its own metadata. The only real fix for that
# is keeping .git out of iCloud's reach.
*\ 2
*\ 2.*
